# Request
# Another robot broadcast a sentence about work it is offering. This asks what
# that sentence means for the bid we were about to make.
#
# This is the one place in the system where text written by a peer reaches a
# decision. The src below is self-asserted and carries no MAC, so the sentence
# could have been written by anyone within radio range. That is survivable only
# because of how narrow the response is: the worst a hostile or confused note
# can do is make this robot bid worse, or not bid. It cannot start an auction,
# take on work, drop work, or move the robot.

# The note, reassembled, as the sender wrote it. Prompt material, never parsed.
string note_text
# Who says they sent it.
uint8  announcer_id
# The announced task the text is about. The join key: there is no such thing
# here as text about nothing in particular.
uint16 task_id

# The offer itself, as it arrived -- so the model can tell a note that adds
# something from a note that restates the fields. Zeroed if the note beat the
# announcement here, which is the intended ordering.
uint16 required_capabilities
uint8  target_kind
int32  target_a
int32  target_b
uint8  priority

# What our own fitness already decided, before reading this. The model is asked
# to adjust a number rather than invent one.
uint16 our_cost
uint16 our_eta_s
bool   our_feasible
# True when we have not assessed the task yet, which makes the three fields
# above meaningless rather than zero.
bool   our_bid_unknown

# There is deliberately no battery or peer list here, unlike InterpretAnomaly.
# The note context the coordinator holds carries neither, and a field the
# caller can only fill with a placeholder is a field the model reads as fact.
# What the battery is worth to this decision is already inside our_cost, which
# fitness computed from it.
---
# Response
# One of exactly three revisions, named by string because ROS IDL has no
# unions. amiga_ros2_coordinator/vocabulary/schema.py is the authority on what
# they mean, and its client refuses anything that is not one of them.
#
#   keep      the note changes nothing; bid as fitness decided
#   revise    the work is harder (or easier) than the offer implied; bid, but
#             adjusted by cost_delta
#   withdraw  do not bid on this at all
#
# withdraw is not a very large revise. A withdrawn bid is silence; a bad bid is
# still an answer that can win an auction nobody better entered.
bool   ok
# Why not, when ok is false. The coordinator treats a failed interpretation as
# "no interpretation available" and bids exactly as fitness decided -- the safe
# direction, and the behaviour the auction had before notes existed.
string error
string revision

# revise only. Relative on purpose: the note is read before, or alongside, the
# announcement it annotates, so an absolute cost would be one the model
# invented. Negative is allowed -- a note can say the job is easier than it
# looks. The coordinator clamps the result into 0..COST_MAX.
int32  cost_delta

# The agent's own account of why. Logged, never parsed.
string reason
string rationale
# The model that produced the revision.
string model
